<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Evo Meals — Cashless School Meals, Kuwait' }) %>
<meta name="description" content="Evo Meals is the cashless meal booking platform for Kuwait's international schools. Book your child's lunch, top up their wallet, and know the moment they've eaten — every tap, timestamped.">
</head>
<body>

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="wrap site-nav">
    <a href="/" class="site-logo"><span>Evo <span class="dot">Meals</span></span></a>
    <nav class="site-links">
      <a href="#menu">Menu</a>
      <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
      <a href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="site-actions">
      <a href="/login" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">Log in</a>
      <a href="/register" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Create account</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap-wide hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-copy" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Made for Kuwait's families</span>
      <h1>Know they ate.<br>Know what they ate.<br><em>Never have to ask.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Evo Meals replaces the morning scramble for lunch money with a wallet, a booking, and a tap. The moment your child collects their meal at the reader, you see it — dish, time, done.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/register" class="btn btn-primary">Create your account</a>
        <a href="#menu" class="btn btn-ghost">See this week's menu</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-proof">
        <span class="proof-label">Trusted by families at</span>
        <div class="schools">
          <span>American Creativity Academy</span>
          <span>Kuwait English School</span>
          <span>The English School</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="tap-demo">
        <div class="tap-card">
          <div class="chip"></div>
          <div class="card-name">Ahmed A.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tap-reader pulse">
          <div class="ripple"></div>
          <div class="ripple delay"></div>
          <div class="reader-ring">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M6 8.5a8 8 0 0 1 12 0M8.5 11a4.5 4.5 0 0 1 7 0M12 14v.01"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="reader-label">MEAL READER · GATE 2</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tap-toast">
          <div class="toast-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" pathLength="1"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="toast-title">Ahmed tapped in — lunch collected</div>
            <div class="toast-sub">12:14 PM · Arabiatta Chicken Pasta</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section origin-section">
  <div class="wrap origin-wrap">
    <div class="origin-mark" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 21s-7-4.35-9.5-9A5.5 5.5 0 0 1 12 6a5.5 5.5 0 0 1 9.5 6c-2.5 4.65-9.5 9-9.5 9Z"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Why we built this</span>
      <h2>Because "did you eat?" shouldn't be a guess.</h2>
      <p class="origin-body">Evo Meals started with a frustration every parent in Kuwait knows — sending your child off with lunch money and just hoping. Hoping it was enough. Hoping they actually ate instead of skipping the line. Hoping the allergy you've mentioned a dozen times was actually remembered by whoever was serving that day. We built the system we wished existed — one that turns all that hoping into something you can actually see, the moment it happens.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-tint" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">How it actually works</span>
      <h2>Four steps, once a term.</h2>
      <p>Set it up once. From then on, lunch just happens — and you find out about it, instead of wondering.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-reveal data-reveal-group="steps">
        <div class="step-num">Book</div>
        <h3>Pick a plan</h3>
        <p>Choose a meal, pay-as-you-go or a flat monthly plan, and the total is calculated and shown before you confirm — never a surprise charge.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-reveal data-reveal-group="steps">
        <div class="step-num">Wallet</div>
        <h3>Top up once</h3>
        <p>Fund the wallet with KNET. Bookings draw from balance automatically — no cash, no forgotten lunch money, ever.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-reveal data-reveal-group="steps">
        <div class="step-num">Tap</div>
        <h3>Your child taps in</h3>
        <p>At the meal counter, their card taps the reader. No PIN, no queue for cash — just a two-second tap they can do themselves.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step" data-reveal data-reveal-group="steps">
        <div class="step-num">Notified</div>
        <h3>You see it happen</h3>
        <p>The moment they tap, your dashboard updates: which meal, and the exact time they collected it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="menu">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">This week's menu</span>
      <h2>Real meals, real nutrition, on the record.</h2>
      <p>Every dish is checked against your child's allergy profile before it's ever offered as an option — not left for you to double-check on the day.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="allergen-row" style="justify-content:center;">
      <span class="allergen-pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Nut-free available</span>
      <span class="allergen-pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Shellfish-free available</span>
      <span class="allergen-pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Sesame-free available</span>
      <span class="allergen-pill"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Soy-free available</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-4">
      <% menuItems.forEach(m => { %>
        <div class="menu-card" data-reveal data-reveal-group="menu">
          <div class="menu-thumb">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M12 2v6M8 8h8l-1 12H9L8 8Z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="menu-card-body">
            <span class="tag"><%= m.tag %></span>
            <h3><%= m.name %></h3>
            <div class="menu-nutri"><span><%= m.calories %> kcal</span><span>·</span><span><%= m.protein %>g protein</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% }) %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="proof-section">
  <div class="wrap-wide proof-wrap">
    <div class="proof-intro" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Where Evo Meals is used</span>
      <p>Not a pilot, not a pitch deck — live at real schools today, booked by real parents, tapped in by real students every school day.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="proof-names">
      <li data-reveal data-reveal-group="proof"><span class="proof-name">American Creativity Academy</span><span class="proof-tag">Partner school</span></li>
      <li data-reveal data-reveal-group="proof"><span class="proof-name">Kuwait English School</span><span class="proof-tag">Partner school</span></li>
      <li data-reveal data-reveal-group="proof"><span class="proof-name">The English School</span><span class="proof-tag">Partner school</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="pricing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
      <h2>One price, shown before you pay.</h2>
      <p>This is the exact total the booking screen calculates — nothing hidden, nothing left blank.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pricing-grid">
      <div class="price-card" data-reveal data-reveal-group="pricing">
        <div class="price-tag">Pay as you go</div>
        <div class="price-amt">KWD <%= (plans.single ? plans.single.rateKWD : 1).toFixed(3) %><span>/day</span></div>
        <p>Book single days whenever you need to — school trips, half terms, or just trying it out.</p>
        <a href="/register" class="btn btn-outline" style="width:100%;">Start booking</a>
      </div>
      <div class="price-card featured" data-reveal data-reveal-group="pricing">
        <span class="badge-save">Most parents choose this</span>
        <div class="price-tag">Monthly plan</div>
        <div class="price-amt">KWD <%= (plans.monthly ? plans.monthly.rateKWD : 24).toFixed(3) %><span>/month</span></div>
        <p><%= plans.monthly ? plans.monthly.monthlyDays : 22 %> school days covered, booked once — works out cheaper than paying daily, and one less thing to remember.</p>
        <a href="/register" class="btn btn-primary" style="width:100%;">Start with the monthly plan</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-tint" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions parents actually ask</span>
      <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary><span>My child has an allergy. How does that get handled?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">You list allergies on their student profile once. Every meal in the ordering flow is checked against that profile, and dishes are labelled nut-, shellfish-, sesame-, and soy-free where they qualify — not left for you to double-check on the day.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span>What if I need to cancel a booking?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Cancel any upcoming booking from your history page before the meal is collected. The full amount is refunded straight back to your wallet — no ticket, no waiting on a refund process.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span>How does the "tap" actually work?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Your child carries a school-issued meal card. At the counter, they tap it against the reader — that single tap confirms their booking, marks the meal collected, and updates your dashboard within moments. No PIN and no cash changes hands.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span>Is my payment information safe?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Wallet top-ups go through KNET, Kuwait's national payment gateway — Evo Meals never stores your card details. Your child's Civil ID is masked everywhere it's shown in the app, including to you.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary><span>Can school staff use Evo Meals too?</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes — staff have their own meal booking flow, separate from student accounts, at a fixed staff meal price.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="wrap-wide cta-inner">
    <div class="cta-copy" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Ready when you are</span>
      <h2>Set it up before<br>the next school run.</h2>
      <p>Takes about two minutes — add a child, top up the wallet, book the first meal.</p>
      <a href="/register" class="btn btn-primary">Create your account</a>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-echo" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="cta-echo-label">This is what you'll see</span>
      <div class="cta-echo-toast">
        <span class="cta-echo-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span>
        <div>
          <div class="cta-echo-title">Ahmed tapped in — lunch collected</div>
          <div class="cta-echo-sub">12:14 PM · Arabiatta Chicken Pasta</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="site-foot">
  <div class="wrap">Evo Meals · cashless school meals for Kuwait</div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
